      "name": "CRT_strpbrk",
      "signature": "char * CRT_strpbrk(char * szString, char * szCharSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Scans string for first occurrence of any character from charset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build 256-bit bitmap (32 bytes on stack) from charset\n2. For each char in charset, set corresponding bit via BTS\n3. Scan input string byte-by-byte\n4. For each char, check bitmap via BT instruction\n5. Return pointer to first matching char, or 0 if none found\n\nParameters:\n- szString (char*): String to scan for matching characters\n- szCharSet (char*): Set of characters to search for\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to first char in szString that exists in szCharSet\n- 0 (NULL cast as char) if no match found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bitmap size for 256 characters (256/8 bits)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0eb6c316488d30b6ee5d8d243ea3c5d6",
