      "name": "InitializeIoFileHandles",
      "signature": "void InitializeIoFileHandles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT I/O file handle table for stdin, stdout, stderr.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate initial I/O info table (0x480 bytes for 32 entries)\n2. Initialize each entry with invalid handle (-1), default flags\n3. Get STARTUPINFO to check for inherited handles from parent\n4. If inherited handles exist, expand table if needed and copy handles\n5. For handles 0-2 (stdin/stdout/stderr), get standard handles via GetStdHandle\n6. Set appropriate flags based on file type (FILE_TYPE_CHAR=0x40, FILE_TYPE_PIPE=0x08)\n7. Call SetHandleCount to notify system of handle count\n\nParameters:\n- (none) - uses global state only\n\nReturns:\n- void - exits via __amsg_exit(0x1b) if malloc fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480: Size per I/O table block (32 entries * 36 bytes)\n- 0x24 (36): Stride per I/O info entry\n- 0x800: Max inherited handles (2048)\n- 0xFFFFFFF6 (-10): STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFF5 (-11): STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xFFFFFFF4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CRTDllMainHandler (caller)",
