      "name": "CloseCrtHandle",
      "signature": "int CloseCrtHandle(uint dwCrtFd)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes a CRT file descriptor and its underlying OS handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get OS handle from CRT fd; if invalid (-1), skip to step 4\n2. For stdout(1)/stderr(2), check if they share the same OS handle\n3. If not shared, call CloseHandle on the OS handle\n4. Invalidate CRT IO handle entry via InvalidateIoHandle\n5. Clear the flags byte at offset 4 in IoInfo structure\n\nParameters:\n- dwCrtFd (uint): CRT file descriptor number (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (sets errno via MapWindowsErrorToErrno)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): IoInfo structure stride in g_apIoInfoTable\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for slot index within group (32 entries per group)\n- 4: Offset to flags byte in IoInfo structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
