      "name": "FreeTlsDataAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void FreeTlsDataAndCleanup(void * pTlsData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Frees thread-local storage data and associated allocations on thread detach.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if TLS index is valid (not 0xFFFFFFFF)\n2. If pTlsData is NULL, get current thread's TLS data via TlsGetValue\n3. Free all non-NULL pointers in TLS structure at offsets 0x24-0x50\n4. Skip freeing offset 0x50 if it points to g_pDefaultTlsData\n5. Free the TLS data structure itself\n6. Clear the TLS slot by setting it to NULL\n\nParameters:\n- pTlsData (void*): TLS data structure to free, or NULL to use current thread's data\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout:\n- +0x24: Allocated buffer 1\n- +0x28: Allocated buffer 2\n- +0x30: Allocated buffer 3\n- +0x38: Allocated buffer 4\n- +0x40: Allocated buffer 5\n- +0x44: Allocated buffer 6\n- +0x50: Default data pointer (skipped if == g_pDefaultTlsData)\n\nCalled By:\n- CRTDllMainHandler on DLL_THREAD_DETACH (reason=3)",
