      "name": "FlushBufferWriteChar",
      "signature": "uint FlushBufferWriteChar(uint dwChar, FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Flushes the file buffer and writes a single character (CRT _flsbuf).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check file mode flags (_flag) for write capability\n2. If read mode with data, reset buffer to base; clear read flag\n3. Set write mode flag (0x2) and clear read flag (0x10)\n4. If unbuffered or special streams (stdin/stdout), allocate buffer\n5. If buffered mode (0x108): flush existing data via write, store char at base\n6. If unbuffered: write single character directly\n7. Return character on success, -1 (EOF) on error\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to write (only low byte used)\n- pFile (FILE*): Pointer to FILE structure\n\nReturns:\n- dwChar & 0xFF on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1/EOF) on error, sets error flag (0x20)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x82: Read mode flags (_IOREAD | _IORW)\n- 0x40: Error flag (_IOERR)\n- 0x20: Error/EOF flag\n- 0x10: End-of-file flag (_IOEOF)\n- 0x108: Buffered modes (_IOFBF | _IOLBF)\n- 0x6fc4e478: stdin FILE structure\n- 0x6fc4e498: stdout FILE structure",
