      "name": "ItoaWrapper",
      "signature": "char * ItoaWrapper(int nValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Wrapper for integer-to-string conversion (itoa) with signed support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if radix is 10 (decimal) and value is negative\n2. If negative decimal, set sign flag to 1 for minus prefix\n3. If not negative or non-decimal, set sign flag to 0\n4. Call ItoaCore with value, buffer, radix, and sign flag\n5. Return buffer pointer for call chaining\n\nParameters:\n- nValue (int): Signed integer value to convert\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for null-terminated ASCII string\n- dwRadix (uint): Numeric base (10=decimal, 16=hex)\n\nReturns:\n- char*: szBuffer pointer (allows function chaining)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc44b48: ItoaCore - does actual conversion with sign handling",
