      "name": "CallocHeapMemory",
      "signature": "void * CallocHeapMemory(uint dwNumElements, uint dwElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and zeroes memory for an array of elements (calloc implementation).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total allocation size: dwNumElements * dwElementSize\n2. Validate size does not exceed 0xFFFFFFE0 (max safe allocation)\n3. Align calculated size up to 16-byte boundary using (size + 0xF) & 0xFFFFFFF0\n4. Select allocation strategy based on g_dwHeapMode:\n   - Mode 3 (SBH): Use small-block heap allocator if size <= g_dwSbhThreshold\n   - Mode 2 (PAGE): Use page allocator if aligned size <= g_dwPageThreshold\n   - Fallback: Use HeapAlloc from g_hCrtHeap with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag\n5. Zero allocated memory block with memset if allocated from SBH/PAGE\n6. On allocation failure, invoke new handler (g_pfnNewHandler) and retry\n\nParameters:\n- dwNumElements (uint): Number of array elements to allocate\n- dwElementSize (uint): Size in bytes of each element\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to zeroed memory block on success\n- NULL: On allocation failure after new handler exhaustion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFE1: Maximum safe allocation size check\n- 0x8: HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag for HeapAlloc\n- 0xF / 0xFFFFFFF0: 16-byte alignment calculation masks\n- 9: CRT critical section index for heap synchronization",
