      "name": "SeekFileHandleInternal",
      "signature": "DWORD SeekFileHandleInternal(uint dwHandle, long lOffset, DWORD dwOrigin)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Seeks to a position in a file via its CRT handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert CRT handle to Win32 HANDLE via FUN_6fc49eac\n2. If invalid handle, set errno=9 (EBADF) and return -1\n3. Call SetFilePointer with offset and origin\n4. If error, translate Windows error via FUN_6fc49da8\n5. On success, clear FEOF flag (0x02) in IoInfo and return new position\n\nParameters:\n- dwHandle (uint): CRT file handle index\n- lOffset (long): Byte offset for seek operation\n- dwOrigin (DWORD): Seek origin (FILE_BEGIN=0, FILE_CURRENT=1, FILE_END=2)\n\nReturns:\n- New file position on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): IoInfo structure stride\n- 0x1F (31): Handle-to-slot mask (32 handles per table)\n- 0x02: FEOF flag in IoInfo.byFlags\n- 9: EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
