      "name": "GetOrAllocTlsData",
      "signature": "DWORD * GetOrAllocTlsData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD *",
      "comment": "Gets or allocates thread-local storage data for current thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current error code via GetLastError\n2. Attempt to get existing TLS data via TlsGetValue\n3. If NULL, allocate 0x74 bytes for new TLS structure\n4. Store in TLS slot via TlsSetValue, initialize via InitTlsDataStruct\n5. Set thread ID at offset 0, mark offset 4 as 0xFFFFFFFF\n6. Restore saved error code and return TLS pointer\n7. Fatal exit (__amsg_exit 0x10) if allocation or TlsSetValue fails\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global g_dwTlsIndex for TLS slot)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to thread-local DWORD array (0x74 bytes)\n- Never returns NULL (fatal exit on failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x74: TLS data structure size\n- 0x10: __amsg_exit code for TLS failure",
