      "name": "AllocateFileBuffer",
      "signature": "void AllocateFileBuffer(uint * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Allocates a 4KB I/O buffer for a FILE structure (CRT _getbuf equivalent).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global buffer allocation counter\n2. Attempt malloc(0x1000) for 4KB buffer\n3. If malloc succeeds: set _base to allocated buffer, set flag 0x8, size 0x1000\n4. If malloc fails: use inline 2-byte buffer at offset 0x14, set flag 0x4, size 2\n5. Reset _cnt to 0, set _ptr to _base\n\nParameters:\n- pFile (uint*): Pointer to FILE structure (offsets: 0=_ptr, 4=_cnt, 8=_base, C=_flag, 18=_bufsiz)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Default buffer size\n- 0x8: Flag indicating dynamically allocated buffer\n- 0x4: Flag indicating inline/small buffer fallback\n- 0x14: Offset to inline 2-byte buffer within FILE struct",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6db4eec4529d7320d9c182be8df08afa",
