      "name": "InitEnvironmentArray",
      "signature": "void InitEnvironmentArray(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the CRT environment variable array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Ensure environment block is initialized (call FUN_6fc49960 if needed)\n2. Count environment strings (skip entries starting with '=')\n3. Allocate pointer array for env count + 1 (NULL terminator)\n4. Copy each valid environment string to new allocation\n5. Free original environment block and NULL the pointer\n6. Set g_fEnvArrayReady flag\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void (calls __amsg_exit(9) on allocation failure)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_ppEnvArray: receives allocated array of env string pointers\n- g_pEnvironment: set to NULL after freeing\n- g_fEnvArrayReady: set to 1 on completion",
