      "name": "CopyStringFast",
      "signature": "char * CopyStringFast(char * lpszDest, char * lpszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Optimized strcpy using DWORD alignment for fast block copying.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check source alignment (lpszSrc & 3)\n2. Copy bytes one at a time until 4-byte aligned\n3. Copy 4 bytes (DWORD) at a time using null detection\n4. Detect null byte in DWORD via magic constant trick\n5. When null found, copy remaining 1-4 bytes and null-terminate\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDest (char*): Destination buffer, must be large enough\n- lpszSrc (char*): Source null-terminated string\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to lpszDest (original destination)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7efefeff: Null byte detection constant for DWORD scan\n- 0x81010100: Result mask for null byte position detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
