      "name": "LockIoHandle",
      "signature": "void LockIoHandle(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Locks the critical section for an I/O handle entry.\n\nUses double-checked locking pattern to lazily initialize\nthe per-handle critical section on first use.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate table index (dwFileHandle >> 5)\n2. Calculate entry offset ((dwFileHandle & 0x1f) * 0x24)\n3. Get pointer to IoInfo entry from g_apIoInfoTable\n4. If critical section not initialized (offset+0x8 == 0):\n   a. Acquire global CRT lock (index 0x11)\n   b. Double-check initialization flag\n   c. Initialize critical section at offset+0xc\n   d. Set initialized flag (offset+0x8)\n   e. Release global CRT lock\n5. Enter the per-handle critical section\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): CRT file handle index\n\nReturns:\n- void (caller must call UnlockIoHandle when done)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f: Mask for entry index (32 entries per table)\n- 0x24: IoInfo structure stride (36 bytes)\n- 0x8: Offset of init flag in IoInfo\n- 0xc: Offset of CRITICAL_SECTION in IoInfo\n- 0x11: Global CRT I/O lock index",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
