      "name": "CompareStringsCaseInsensitive",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsCaseInsensitive(void * this, byte * pbStr1, byte * pbStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive string comparison with locale support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If locale mode disabled (DAT_6fc50d00 == 0):\n   - Simple ASCII case-insensitive compare\n   - Converts A-Z to lowercase via arithmetic\n2. If locale mode enabled:\n   - Increments thread lock counter\n   - Enters critical section if needed (index 0x13)\n   - Converts each differing char via FUN_6fc45fe3 (locale tolower)\n   - Decrements lock or leaves critical section\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Object context (unused in simple mode)\n- pbStr1 (byte*): First null-terminated string\n- pbStr2 (byte*): Second null-terminated string\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Strings are equal\n- -1: pbStr1 < pbStr2\n- 1: pbStr1 > pbStr2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xBF (-65): Offset to normalize 'A' (0x41) to 0\n- 0x1A (26): Number of uppercase letters\n- 0x20 (32): Uppercase to lowercase offset\n- 0x13 (19): Critical section index for locale operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8c1ef08c13327b78f680f81ff5d26364",
