      "name": "Int64ToCharWithSign",
      "signature": "char * Int64ToCharWithSign(uint dwValueLo, int nValueHi, char * lpszBuffer, uint dwRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts a signed 64-bit integer to a character string with sign handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize negative flag to 0 (assume positive)\n2. Check if radix is decimal (0xA) for signed interpretation\n3. Check if high word indicates negative (nValueHi < 0)\n4. If both conditions met, set negative flag to 1\n5. Call Int64ToCharCore with value, buffer, radix, and sign flag\n6. Return the buffer pointer for call chaining\n\nParameters:\n- dwValueLo (uint): Low 32 bits of the 64-bit integer value\n- nValueHi (int): High 32 bits, signed to detect negative numbers\n- lpszBuffer (char*): Output buffer for the resulting string\n- dwRadix (uint): Number base for conversion (2-36, typically 10 or 16)\n\nReturns:\n- lpszBuffer pointer, allowing chained string operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9054131dac4db9c694bbfb145a573d3e",
