      "name": "RegisterAtExitFunction",
      "signature": "void * RegisterAtExitFunction(void * pfnAtExitHandler)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Registers a function to be called during program exit (atexit implementation).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire exit critical section lock\n2. Check if array has space for new entry\n3. If full, reallocate with +16 bytes capacity\n4. If realloc fails, return NULL (failure)\n5. Store function pointer at end of array\n6. Increment array end pointer by 4 bytes\n7. Release lock and return the registered function pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pfnAtExitHandler (void*): Function pointer to call at exit\n\nReturns:\n- Non-NULL: Success (returns the registered function pointer)\n- NULL: Failure (reallocation failed)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- LockExitCriticalSection: Acquires thread safety lock\n- UnlockExitCriticalSection: Releases thread safety lock\n- FUN_6fc463dd: Gets current allocation size\n- FUN_6fc460ae: Reallocates memory buffer",
