      "name": "MoveMemory",
      "signature": "void * MoveMemory(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint dwBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Copies dwBytes from pSrc to pDest, handling overlapping memory regions.\nStandard memmove implementation that detects overlap and uses reverse copy if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if regions overlap (pSrc < pDest < pSrc+dwBytes)\n2. If overlap detected, copy backward from end to start\n3. If no overlap, copy forward from start to end\n4. Align destination to 4-byte boundary for DWORD copies\n5. Copy bulk data using REP MOVSD (32-bit moves)\n6. Handle trailing 1-3 bytes individually via switch table\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer address\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer address\n- dwBytes (uint): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- pDest: Original destination pointer (for chaining)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Alignment mask for DWORD boundary\n- 0x8: Threshold for bulk MOVSD optimization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
