      "name": "LCMapStringWithLocale",
      "signature": "int LCMapStringWithLocale(LCID dwLocaleId, uint dwMapFlags, char * lpszSrcStr, int nSrcLen, LPWSTR lpwszDestStr, int nDestLen, UINT uCodePage, int nUseFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Performs locale-aware string mapping with automatic Unicode/ANSI conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception frame for stack allocation protection\n2. On first call, detect locale mapping support by testing LCMapStringW/A\n3. Set g_dwLocaleMapMode: 1=Wide, 2=ANSI\n4. If nSrcLen > 0, compute actual length via GetMultiByteStringLength\n5. For ANSI mode: call LCMapStringA directly\n6. For Wide mode: convert MB to WC, map via LCMapStringW\n7. If LCMAP_SORTKEY (0x400) not set, convert WC back to MB\n8. Return result length or 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n- dwLocaleId (LCID): Windows locale identifier\n- dwMapFlags (uint): LCMAP_* flags (0x100=lowercase, 0x400=sortkey)\n- lpszSrcStr (char*): Source multibyte string\n- nSrcLen (int): Source length (-1 for null-terminated)\n- lpwszDestStr (LPWSTR): Destination buffer\n- nDestLen (int): Destination size (0 to query)\n- uCodePage (UINT): Code page (0 uses default)\n- nUseFlags (int): Non-zero adds MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS\n\nReturns:\n- Number of chars/bytes written on success\n- 0 on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: LCMAP_LOWERCASE\n- 0x400: LCMAP_SORTKEY\n- 0x220: WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS | WC_COMPOSITECHECK",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
