      "name": "InvalidateIoHandle",
      "signature": "int InvalidateIoHandle(uint dwHandleIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Invalidates and clears an I/O handle entry in the CRT I/O table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate handle index against g_dwIoHandleCount\n2. Compute table slot: index >> 5 for array, (index & 0x1f) * 0x24 for offset\n3. Check handle is valid (flag bit 0 set, value != -1)\n4. If error mode is 1 and handle is stdin/stdout/stderr (0/1/2), call SetStdHandle with NULL\n5. Set handle value to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) to invalidate\n6. On invalid handle, set errno to EBADF (9) via TLS\n\nParameters:\n- dwHandleIndex (uint): CRT file handle index (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success, handle invalidated\n- -1: Invalid handle index or handle not open\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): I/O info structure stride\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for slot within segment (32 handles per segment)\n- 0xfffffff6 (-10): STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xfffffff5 (-11): STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE\n- 0xfffffff4 (-12): STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n- 9: EBADF errno value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
