      "name": "WriteFileInternal",
      "signature": "int WriteFileInternal(uint dwFileHandle, char * szBuffer, uint dwCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Writes data to a file handle with text-mode LF to CRLF translation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If count is 0, return 0 immediately\n2. Look up IoInfo from g_apIoInfoTable using handle index\n3. If append mode (0x20 flag), seek to end of file\n4. If binary mode (0x80 not set), call WriteFile directly\n5. If text mode (0x80 set), process in 1024-byte chunks:\n   a. Copy bytes to temp buffer, inserting CR before each LF\n   b. Call WriteFile for each filled chunk\n   c. Track CR additions to adjust return value\n6. On success, return bytes written minus added CRs\n7. On error, set errno/doserrno and return -1\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): CRT file handle index\n- szBuffer (char*): Source data buffer to write\n- dwCount (uint): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes written (adjusted for CR additions) on success\n- 0 if count was 0\n- -1 on error (errno set)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): IoInfo structure stride\n- 0x20: Append mode flag (O_APPEND)\n- 0x80: Text mode flag (O_TEXT)\n- 0x40: Ctrl-Z EOF flag\n- 0x400 (1024): Text-mode conversion buffer size\n- 0x1a (26): Ctrl-Z EOF character\n\nRelated Functions:\n- WriteValidateHandle: Caller that validates handle\n- SeekFileHandleInternal: Used for append mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
