      "name": "ToLowerWithLocale",
      "signature": "uint ToLowerWithLocale(void * this, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts a character to lowercase using locale-specific rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If no locale codepage (g_dwLocaleCodePage == 0):\n   - ASCII range: 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5A) -> add 0x20 to lowercase\n   - Non-ASCII: return unchanged\n2. If locale enabled and char < 0x100:\n   - Check g_pwCharTypeTable for uppercase flag (bit 0)\n   - If g_dwLocaleMode >= 2, use GetCharTypeFlags\n   - If not uppercase, return unchanged\n3. For uppercase chars:\n   - Single-byte or DBCS detection via high-bit check\n   - Call FUN_6fc47f38 (LCMapString wrapper) to convert\n   - Extract 1 or 2 byte result from wLower\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Object context (unused)\n- dwChar (uint): Character to convert (may be DBCS)\n\nReturns:\n- Lowercase character value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41/0x5A: 'A'/'Z' ASCII range\n- 0x20: Uppercase to lowercase offset\n- 0x100: Single-byte threshold\n- 0x80: DBCS lead byte indicator in char type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
