      "name": "ConvertStringToLong",
      "signature": "long ConvertStringToLong(void * this, byte * pbInput, int * pnEndPtr, int nBase, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "long",
      "comment": "Converts a string to a long integer with base detection and overflow handling.\nCore implementation for strtol() CRT function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace using locale-aware character type check\n2. Parse optional sign (+ sets positive, - sets negative flag)\n3. Auto-detect base if nBase=0: 0x prefix->16, 0 prefix->8, else->10\n4. Validate base is in range [2..36], return 0 if invalid\n5. Skip 0x/0X prefix for base 16\n6. Parse digits: 0-9 for values 0-9, A-Z/a-z via toupper for 10-35\n7. Accumulate result with overflow detection using max/base threshold\n8. On overflow, set errno=ERANGE and clamp to LONG_MAX/LONG_MIN\n9. Store end pointer and apply sign negation if needed\n\nParameters:\n- pbInput (byte*): Input string to parse\n- pnEndPtr (int*): Receives pointer to first unconverted char, NULL if not needed\n- nBase (int): Number base: 0 for auto-detect, or 2-36\n- dwFlags (uint): Parsing flags - bit 1=negative, bit 2=unsigned, bit 3=has_digits\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed long value on success\n- 0 if no valid digits or invalid base\n- LONG_MAX (0x7FFFFFFF) on positive overflow\n- LONG_MIN (0x80000000) on negative overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2d (45): ASCII '-' minus sign\n- 0x2b (43): ASCII '+' plus sign\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0' for octal/hex prefix detection\n- 0x58/0x78: ASCII 'X'/'x' for hex prefix\n- 0x24 (36): Maximum valid base\n- 0x22 (34): ERANGE errno value for overflow",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cf4bba8373cc6f7fefec3dac17cb97f9",
