      "name": "FindPageBlockEntry",
      "signature": "int FindPageBlockEntry(byte * pbBlock, void * * ppRegion, uint * pdwPageBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Finds page block entry for a pointer in the page-based heap system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search linked list of heap regions starting at g_pSbhRegionHead\n2. Check if pbBlock falls within each region's address range [+0x10, +0x14]\n3. Validate pointer is 16-byte aligned (pbBlock & 0xF == 0)\n4. Validate page offset >= 0x100 (pbBlock & 0xFFF >= 0x100)\n5. Output region pointer and page base address\n6. Calculate and return block entry index\n\nParameters:\n- pbBlock (byte*): Memory block pointer to look up\n- ppRegion (void**): Output - receives pointer to containing region\n- pdwPageBase (uint*): Output - receives page base address (block & 0xFFFFF000)\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero entry address on success (page_base + index + 8)\n- 0 if block not found or invalid alignment\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0F: 16-byte alignment mask\n- 0xFFF: Page offset mask (4KB)\n- 0x100 (256): Minimum valid page offset\n- 0xFFFFF000: Page base mask\n- 0x10, 0x14: Region structure offsets for address range",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
