      "name": "ReallocWithHeapStrategy",
      "signature": "byte * ReallocWithHeapStrategy(byte * pbBlock, uint dwNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Reallocates memory using strategy based on heap type mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pbBlock is NULL, allocate new memory via _malloc\n2. If nNewSize is 0, free the block via FUN_6fc4719c\n3. Otherwise select strategy based on DAT_6fc52208 heap mode:\n   - Mode 3 (SBH): Use small-block heap with lock/copy/free\n   - Mode 2 (Page): Use page-based heap with 16-byte alignment\n   - Default: Direct HeapReAlloc with 16-byte rounding\n4. On allocation failure, invoke new handler if registered\n\nParameters:\n- pbBlock (byte*): Existing memory block to reallocate, or NULL for new alloc\n- nNewSize (uint): Requested new size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to reallocated block on success\n- NULL on failure (after exhausting new handler retries)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFE0: Max valid size check (~4GB - 32)\n- 0x0F: Alignment mask for 16-byte rounding\n- 9: Critical section index for heap operations\n- 3: Small-block heap mode\n- 2: Page-based heap mode",
