      "name": "AllocFromSmallBlockHeap",
      "signature": "void * AllocFromSmallBlockHeap(uint dwBlockSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from the Small Block Heap (SBH).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start with cached current region pointer\n2. Check if region has valid page mapping (offset != -1)\n3. Search from cached position to end of region for suitable block\n4. If not found, search from start of region to cached position\n5. If block found with sufficient space, allocate via FUN_6fc491ce\n6. If no block found, traverse circular region list\n7. If traversed all regions, look for expandable region\n8. Expand region with VirtualAlloc if possible\n9. If no expandable region, create new region via CreateSmallBlockHeapRegion\n10. Initialize allocated pages and update region bookkeeping\n11. Return pointer to user data area (offset +0x100 from block header)\n\nParameters:\n- dwBlockSize (uint): Size in allocation units (0x10-byte granularity)\n\nReturns:\n- void* to allocated memory on success\n- NULL if VirtualAlloc fails or CreateSmallBlockHeapRegion fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2018: Region boundary offset (0x806 * 8 + 0x18)\n- 0x1000: Page size (4KB) for VirtualAlloc\n- 0xF0 (240): Maximum block units\n- 0xF1 (241): Block high watermark sentinel\n- 0x100 (256): User data offset from block header\n- 0x10: Max pages to commit at once\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fc491ce: Allocate from specific block\n- CreateSmallBlockHeapRegion: Create new region",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
