      "name": "ToUpperWithLocale",
      "signature": "uint ToUpperWithLocale(int nChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Converts lowercase ASCII letter to uppercase with locale support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale is disabled (g_dwLocaleCodePage == 0)\n2. If no locale, check if char in 'a'-'z' range (0x61-0x7a)\n3. If lowercase, subtract 0x20 to convert to uppercase\n4. If locale active, acquire lock via InterlockedIncrement\n5. Check if lock limit set for critical section mode\n6. Call CharToUpperWithLocale for locale-aware conversion\n7. Release lock appropriately and return result\n\nParameters:\n- nChar (int): Character code to convert\n\nReturns:\n- Uppercase character code if input was lowercase ASCII\n- Original character code otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60 (96): One less than 'a' for range check\n- 0x7b (123): One more than 'z' for range check\n- 0x20 (32): ASCII difference between cases\n- 0x13 (19): CRT critical section index",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
