      "name": "GetEnvironmentBlockCopy",
      "signature": "char * GetEnvironmentBlockCopy(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Returns a malloc'd copy of the environment block in ANSI format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nEnvStringsType cached state (0=unknown, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n2. If unknown, try GetEnvironmentStringsW first\n3. If Unicode available, convert to ANSI via WideCharToMultiByte\n4. If Unicode fails, fall back to GetEnvironmentStringsA\n5. Copy environment block to malloc'd buffer\n6. Free original environment strings and return copy\n\nParameters:\n- (none) - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to malloc'd ANSI environment block copy\n- NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: Unknown environment string type\n- 1: Unicode environment strings available\n- 2: ANSI environment strings only",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
