      "name": "InvokeNewHandler",
      "signature": "bool InvokeNewHandler(uint dwRequestedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Invokes the registered new handler callback when memory allocation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pfnNewHandler callback is registered (non-NULL)\n2. If registered, call the handler with the requested allocation size\n3. Return true if handler returns non-zero (signals retry), false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- dwRequestedSize (uint): Size in bytes that failed to allocate\n\nReturns:\n- true: Handler succeeded, caller should retry allocation\n- false: No handler registered or handler failed\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CallocHeapMemory, __nh_malloc: Callers that retry allocation on true",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
