      "name": "SbhAllocateBlock",
      "signature": "void * SbhAllocateBlock(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from the Small Block Heap (SBH) free lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round up size to 16-byte alignment, calculate bucket index\n2. Build bitmask pair (dwMaskLow/dwMaskHigh) for bucket availability\n3. Search heap blocks starting from g_pSbhBlockCurrent for available buckets\n4. If no suitable block found, try remaining blocks or create new block via SbhCreateBlock\n5. Locate free list entry matching bucket, remove from free list\n6. Split block if remainder is large enough, insert remainder in appropriate bucket\n7. Mark allocated block with size+1 sentinel at header and footer\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize: Requested allocation size in bytes (before alignment)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to usable memory (after 4-byte header), or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17 (23): Alignment overhead for 16-byte boundary\n- 0x14 (20): Stride of heap block descriptor array (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x81 (129): Page descriptor stride in the region header\n- 0x3f (63): Maximum bucket index (64 buckets total)\n\nStructure:\n- Block header/footer store size|1 (low bit marks allocated)\n- Free blocks use doubly-linked list with fwd/bwd pointers at +4/+8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
