      "name": "ReadFileAndValidate",
      "signature": "void ReadFileAndValidate(uint dwHandle, int nBytesToRead, uint dwBuffer, int nExpectedBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reads file data via Storm and validates bytes read matches expected.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert file handle is valid (nBytesToRead != 0)\n2. Save expected byte count before read\n3. Call SFileReadFile (Ordinal_10104) to read data\n4. If read fails, copy file path and log error\n5. Assert bytes read equals expected bytes\n\nParameters:\n- dwHandle (uint): Storm file handle (ECX)\n- nBytesToRead (int): Bytes to read (EDX), used as file handle validator\n- dwBuffer (uint): Destination buffer for read data\n- nExpectedBytes (int): Expected bytes to read, updated with actual\n\nReturns:\n- void (asserts on failure via FUN_6fc44a19)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size for error string\n- 0x87: Source line for hFile assertion\n- 0x8f: Source line for read failure log\n- 0x92: Source line for byte count mismatch assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
