      "name": "GetHeapSelectionMode",
      "signature": "int GetHeapSelectionMode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Determines heap allocation mode based on OS version and environment settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check Windows version via GetVersionExA\n2. If Windows 2000+ (platform 2, version 5+), return mode 1\n3. Otherwise check __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n4. Convert env var to uppercase and parse for heap mode selection\n5. If __GLOBAL_HEAP_SELECTED prefix found, use global heap\n6. Otherwise search for current module name in env var\n7. Parse comma-separated heap mode value after module name\n8. Return parsed mode (1/2/3) or default based on result\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Use system heap (Windows 2000+ default)\n- 2: Use old heap mode\n- 3: Use default heap mode (fallback)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x94 (148): sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA)\n- 0x16 (22): Length of __GLOBAL_HEAP_SELECTED\n- 0x2c (44): Comma character delimiter\n- 0x3b (59): Semicolon terminator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
