      "name": "ProcessFormatString",
      "signature": "int ProcessFormatString(int * pnOutputCtrl, byte * pbFormat, uint * pdwArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses sprintf-style format string and outputs formatted result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse format string character by character using state machine\n2. State 0: Copy literal text to output\n3. State 1: '%' detected, initialize format parsing\n4. State 2: Parse flags (-, +, #, 0, space)\n5. State 3: Parse width (digits or *)\n6. State 4: '.' detected, start precision\n7. State 5: Parse precision (digits or *)\n8. State 6: Parse length modifier (h, l, w, I64)\n9. State 7: Format specifier - process and output value\n\nParameters:\n- pnOutputCtrl (int*): Output control struct with buffer ptr\n- pbFormat (byte*): Format string to parse\n- pdwArgs (uint*): Varargs pointer\n\nReturns:\n- Chars written on success, negative on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8000: FL_I64 (64-bit integer)\n- 0x800: FL_WIDE (wide char mode)\n- 0x200: FL_OCTAL_PREFIX\n- 0x100: FL_NEGATIVE\n- 0x80: FL_ALTERNATE (#)\n- 0x40: FL_SIGNED (d/i)\n- 0x20: FL_SHORT (h)\n- 0x10: FL_LONG (l)\n- 0x08: FL_ZERO (0)\n- 0x04: FL_LEFT (-)\n- 0x02: FL_SPACE\n- 0x01: FL_PLUS (+)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
